oblem of what lab researches. Might be paradigm breaking (4). Could be paradigm stretching (3). The definition: 4 introduces new elements AND changes the relationship... or addresses larger problem of what the lab researches. It does both. So 4.\n\nOriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious, imaginative, surprising\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common\n\nIs building toolkit from logs for drift detection... Unusual? Possibly interesting but maybe common. Using compliance logs as research data is somewhat unusual, imaginative. Might be 3? \"not expressed before AND ingenious\" maybe too strong. Could be unusual, interesting; shows some imagination => 3.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4):\ndegree to which idea will solve problem.\nProblem: AI R&D lab must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources to pursue proposal, not funding to explore whether idea might someday work.\n\nDoes proposal solve logging mandate? It builds toolkit using logs, partners to collect anonymised log corpora. Does it ensure compliance with Article 12 logging? It treats logs as research data but doesn't explicitly ensure logging capabilities are implemented per Article 12.1-3. Might contribute to post-market monitoring and traceability, which is related. But effectiveness at solving problem of meeting logging mandate? It leverages mandated logs, so indirectly helps meet mandate by creating value from them, but does it ensure compliance? Probably will contribute to solution, not fully solve mandate implementation. Might be 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial solution). Could be 4 if it solves stated problem without regard for workability. Stated problem: must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal adapts R&D to use logs, so addresses adaptation part. Might solve main problem? Hmm.\n\nThe problem includes meet logging mandate. Proposal doesn't describe implementing logging infrastructure, just using logs. So maybe partial. Effectiveness = 3.\n\nApplicability (1-4):\ndegree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related\n3 = solves implied problem related\nProposal does X: build toolkit using mandated logs -> get Y: research value and risk flagging. Y is part of stated problem? Stated problem is meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Adapting R&D is directly related. So applicability 4? Might be solves identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes: adapts R&D to compliance data.\n\nImplementability (1-4):\ndegree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nBuild open-source statistical toolkit, partner with post-market monitoring unit to collect anonymised log corpora from pilot deployments, develop change-detection algorithms... That's some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Not easy low cost? Requires partnership, data access, anonymisation compliance. Might be some changes, or reasonably feasible measures => 3. Could be significant change expensive/difficult but not impossible =>2. Probably 3.\n\nAcceptability (1-4):\ndegree to which idea is socially, legally, politically acceptable.\nOpen-source toolkit, anonymised logs, partner with post-market monitoring. No violation. Common strategies? Somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities => 3? Or common strategies that violate no norms =>4. Using anonymised logs for research likely acceptable. Open-source is fine. Might be 4 = common strategies that violate no norms. Hmm.\n\nIt involves collecting log corpora from pilot deployments, anonymised. Could raise privacy concerns but anonymised. Probably acceptable. I think 4.\n\nLet's output in required format.\n\nNeed for each subscale: FIRST write one sentence evidence then give score.\n\nProbably format:\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: \"...\"\nparadigm_relatedness: 4\n...\n\nEnsure order listed: paradigm_relatedness, originality, effectiveness, applicability, implementability, acceptability\n\nProvide id echo.\n\nLet's produce final answer.\n\n",
